.TH TGLFS-DOWNLOAD 1 "March 2026" "tglfs 0.1.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tglfs-download \- download a TGLFS file or indexed archive by UFID
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tglfs download
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIufid\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Looks up a TGLFS file card in Telegram Saved Messages by UFID, downloads the encrypted chunks, decrypts and decompresses them, verifies the UFID, and writes the plaintext to disk. File-card versions 1 through 4 are supported. Version 4 archives are reconstructed as the exact original tar using bounded memory. Unsupported future protocol versions are refused.
.PP
Use
.B --legacy
for files that still require the older counter-advance behavior. This option is refused for version 4 indexed archives.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-interactive
Disable interactive prompts and fail instead of prompting.
.TP
.B --output <path>
Destination path for the restored plaintext file.
.TP
.B --force
Overwrite an existing output file.
.TP
.B --legacy
Use the legacy decryption pipeline.
.TP
.B --password <password>
Decryption password.
.TP
.B --password-env [name]
Read the decryption password from an environment variable. If no name is provided, the command uses
.B TGLFS_DOWNLOAD_PASSWORD.
.TP
.B --password-stdin
Read the decryption password from standard input.
.TP
.B --json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TGLFS_DOWNLOAD_PASSWORD
Default environment variable for the decryption password.
.SH AI AGENT NOTES
If the download password is missing and the command is attached to a TTY, the CLI prompts for it. In a non-interactive session, the agent must provide the password via flags, environment variables, or standard input.
Interactive TTY runs also render a progress bar while the file is being restored.
.B --json
prints exactly one final JSON object to standard output, writes failures to standard error, and never prompts.
